It is late now.
Nina says goodnight and leaves.
I turn off the big ceiling light.
Only the lamp by the window is on.
It gives a warm light.
I am lying in my own bed.
There is a blanket on the bed.
The flat is dark and quiet.
I look at the photo of my family.
It is standing on the shelf by the bed.
I think about my home in Mexico.
But I look around the room.
It is good here.
The small flat is also my home now.
"This is my home," I think.
I smile.
